## Overview

Derived memo metadata lives in `store.Memo.Payload` (`MemoPayload` in proto). **Content-derived fields** are `tags` and `property`; **`location` is user-set** via the API and is not computed from markdown. Computation is centralized in `memopayload.RebuildMemoPayload`, which calls `markdown.Service.ExtractAll` on memo content.

---

## Schema: what is stored in `MemoPayload`

```7:28:proto/store/memo.proto
message MemoPayload {
  Property property = 1;

  Location location = 2;

  repeated string tags = 3;

  // The calculated properties from the memo content.
  message Property {
    bool has_link = 1;
    bool has_task_list = 2;
    bool has_code = 3;
    bool has_incomplete_tasks = 4;
    // The title extracted from the first H1 heading, if present.
    string title = 5;
  }

  message Location {
    string placeholder = 1;
    double latitude = 2;
    double longitude = 3;
  }
}
```

API exposes the same derived fields as output-only on `Memo`:

```240:278:proto/api/v1/memo_service.proto
  // Output only. The tags extracted from the content.
  repeated string tags = 10 [(google.api.field_behavior) = OUTPUT_ONLY];
  ...
  // Output only. The computed properties of the memo.
  Property property = 15 [(google.api.field_behavior) = OUTPUT_ONLY];
  ...
  message Property {
    bool has_link = 1;
    bool has_task_list = 2;
    bool has_code = 3;
    bool has_incomplete_tasks = 4;
    // The title extracted from the first H1 heading, if present.
    string title = 5;
  }
```

---

## Where computation happens

### 1. Entry point: `RebuildMemoPayload`

```74:87:server/runner/memopayload/runner.go
func RebuildMemoPayload(_ context.Context, memo *store.Memo, markdownService markdown.Service) error {
	if memo.Payload == nil {
		memo.Payload = &storepb.MemoPayload{}
	}

	// Use goldmark service to extract all metadata in a single pass (more efficient)
	data, err := markdownService.ExtractAll([]byte(memo.Content))
	if err != nil {
		return errors.Wrap(err, "failed to extract markdown metadata")
	}

	memo.Payload.Tags = data.Tags
	memo.Payload.Property = data.Property
	return nil
}
```

Only **`Tags`** and **`Property`** are written. **`Location` is left unchanged** if already present.

### 2. Core extraction: `ExtractAll` (goldmark AST walk)

`MarkdownService` is constructed with GFM + tag + mention extensions:

```47:51:server/router/api/v1/v1.go
	markdownService := markdown.NewService(
		markdown.WithTagExtension(),
		markdown.WithMentionExtension(),
	)
```

Single-pass AST walk in `ExtractAll`:

```355:421:internal/markdown/markdown.go
func (s *service) ExtractAll(content []byte) (*ExtractedData, error) {
	root, err := s.parse(content)
	...
	data := &ExtractedData{
		Tags:     []string{},
		Mentions: []string{},
		Property: &storepb.MemoPayload_Property{},
	}

	firstBlockChecked := false

	// Single walk to collect all data
	err = gast.Walk(root, func(n gast.Node, entering bool) (gast.WalkStatus, error) {
		if !entering {
			return gast.WalkContinue, nil
		}

		if tagNode, ok := asMemoTagNode(n); ok {
			data.Tags = append(data.Tags, string(tagNode.Tag))
		}
		if mentionNode, ok := n.(*mast.MentionNode); ok {
			data.Mentions = append(data.Mentions, strings.ToLower(string(mentionNode.Username)))
		}

		// Check if the first block-level child of the document is an H1 heading.
		if !firstBlockChecked && n.Parent() != nil && n.Parent().Kind() == gast.KindDocument {
			firstBlockChecked = true
			if heading, ok := n.(*gast.Heading); ok && heading.Level == 1 {
				data.Property.Title = extractHeadingText(n, content)
			}
		}

		// Extract properties based on node kind
		switch n.Kind() {
		case gast.KindLink:
			data.Property.HasLink = true

		case gast.KindCodeBlock, gast.KindFencedCodeBlock, gast.KindCodeSpan:
			data.Property.HasCode = true

		case east.KindTaskCheckBox:
			data.Property.HasTaskList = true
			if checkBox, ok := n.(*east.TaskCheckBox); ok {
				if !checkBox.IsChecked {
					data.Property.HasIncompleteTasks = true
				}
			}
		default:
			// No special handling for other node types
		}

		return gast.WalkContinue, nil
	})
	...
	data.Tags = uniquePreserveCase(data.Tags)
	data.Mentions = uniquePreserveCase(data.Mentions)

	return data, nil
}
```

Tags inside links/images are excluded:

```122:140:internal/markdown/markdown.go
func isTagNodeInLinkOrImage(n gast.Node) bool {
	for parent := n.Parent(); parent != nil; parent = parent.Parent() {
		switch parent.Kind() {
		case gast.KindLink, gast.KindImage:
			return true
		default:
			// Keep walking ancestors.
		}
	}
	return false
}

func asMemoTagNode(n gast.Node) (*mast.TagNode, bool) {
	tagNode, ok := n.(*mast.TagNode)
	if !ok || isTagNodeInLinkOrImage(n) {
		return nil, false
	}
	return tagNode, true
}
```

Title text is plain text from the heading subtree:

```172:189:internal/markdown/markdown.go
func extractHeadingText(n gast.Node, source []byte) string {
	var buf strings.Builder
	for child := n.FirstChild(); child != nil; child = child.NextSibling() {
		extractTextFromNode(child, source, &buf)
	}
	return buf.String()
}
```

`ExtractProperties` and `ExtractTags` implement the same property/tag logic separately but are **not** used by `RebuildMemoPayload` (only `ExtractAll` is).

---

## Payload properties extracted from markdown AST/content

| Field | AST / rule | Written to `MemoPayload`? |
|---|---|---|
| `tags` | `#tag` → `TagNode`; deduped, case preserved; skipped inside `Link`/`Image` | Yes |
| `property.has_link` | Any `KindLink` node | Yes |
| `property.has_code` | `KindCodeBlock`, `KindFencedCodeBlock`, or `KindCodeSpan` | Yes |
| `property.has_task_list` | GFM `TaskCheckBox` (`east.KindTaskCheckBox`) | Yes |
| `property.has_incomplete_tasks` | Unchecked `TaskCheckBox` | Yes |
| `property.title` | Plain text of first document block child if it is H1 (`heading.Level == 1`) | Yes |
| `mentions` (in `ExtractedData`) | `@username` → `MentionNode`, lowercased, deduped | **No** — not persisted in payload |
| `location.*` | — | **No** — user-set via API |

---

## Production callers of `RebuildMemoPayload`

There are exactly **two production call sites** (plus one inside an unused runner):

### CreateMemo — always, after length check, before DB insert

```101:113:server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go
	contentLengthLimit, err := s.getContentLengthLimit(ctx)
	...
	if len(create.Content) > contentLengthLimit {
		return nil, status.Errorf(codes.InvalidArgument, "content too long (max %d characters)", contentLengthLimit)
	}
	if err := memopayload.RebuildMemoPayload(ctx, create, s.MarkdownService); err != nil {
		return nil, status.Errorf(codes.Internal, "failed to rebuild memo payload: %v", err)
	}
	if request.Memo.Location != nil {
		create.Payload.Location = convertLocationToStore(request.Memo.Location)
	}
```

**Conditions:** authenticated user; valid UID; content within length limit. No content-change gate — every create rebuilds payload.

**Indirect path:** `CreateMemoComment` delegates to `CreateMemo` (`memo_service_comments.go:56–59`), so comments get the same rebuild.

### UpdateMemo — only when update mask includes `"content"`

```435:451:server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go
	for _, path := range request.UpdateMask.Paths {
		if path == "content" {
			contentUpdated = true
			previousContent = memo.Content
			...
			memo.Content = request.Memo.Content
			if err := memopayload.RebuildMemoPayload(ctx, memo, s.MarkdownService); err != nil {
				return nil, status.Errorf(codes.Internal, "failed to rebuild memo payload: %v", err)
			}
			update.Content = &memo.Content
			update.Payload = memo.Payload
```

**Conditions:** memo exists; creator or superuser; update mask required; `"content"` path; new content within length limit.

**Does not rebuild** for other mask paths (`visibility`, `pinned`, `state`, `create_time`, `update_time`, `location`, `attachments`, `relations`). Location updates patch payload without recomputing tags/properties:

```481:484:server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go
		} else if path == "location" {
			payload := memo.Payload
			payload.Location = convertLocationToStore(request.Memo.Location)
			update.Payload = payload
```

After content update, mentions are re-resolved separately (not stored in payload):

```510:512:server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go
	if contentUpdated {
		s.dispatchMemoMentionNotificationsBestEffort(ctx, memo, parentMemo, previousContent)
	}
```

That path calls `ExtractAll` again via `resolveMentionTargets`:

```26:37:server/router/api/v1/memo_mention_helpers.go
func (s *APIV1Service) resolveMentionTargets(ctx context.Context, content string) (map[int32]*store.User, error) {
	...
	data, err := s.MarkdownService.ExtractAll([]byte(content))
	...
	if len(data.Mentions) == 0 {
		return targets, nil
	}
```

